#
# Usage:
#   Copy this file to deploy.conf and update with your Pi's actual values:
#     cp deploy/deploy.conf.example deploy/deploy.conf
#
#   deploy.conf is gitignored and will not be committed.
#
# Sourced by deploy/deploy-pi.sh (Pi tier).
# Variables here override the script defaults; unset variables fall through to
# the defaults baked into the script.
# ==============================================================================

# Raspberry Pi 5 (chi-eclipse-01) connection details
# ADDRESS THE PI BY HOSTNAME, never a hardcoded IP (CIO directive 2026-08-17).
# ~/.ssh/config is the single HostName+User acquisition point, so one edit there
# follows everywhere. PI_HOST is only ever used for ssh/rsync in deploy-pi.sh,
# so the alias is sufficient -- it does not require network-wide DNS.
# Static fixed IPs behind the aliases (2026-08-15, B-102/US-473 -- ends the
# .28/.100/.9/.27 DHCP flap):
#   chi-eclipse-01      -> 10.27.27.124  WiFi/wlan0, primary headless interface
#   chi-eclipse-01-eth  -> 10.27.27.123  eth0, usually unplugged
PI_HOST=chi-eclipse-01
PI_USER=mcornelison
PI_PATH=/home/mcornelison/Projects/Eclipse-01
PI_PORT=22
